# The Trading Expedition
# A multi-city trading quest spanning Lumbridge, Varrock, and Al Kharid
# 10 objectives - approximately 5x longer than Pest Control

quest trading_expedition
name The Trading Expedition

# NPCs involved in this quest
start_npc hans
npc hans varrock_trader varrock_bartender alkharid_silk alkharid_spice

# === OBJECTIVES (10 total) ===
# 1. Travel to Varrock and talk to Zaff
objective talk_to varrock_trader

# 2. Zaff sends you to the bartender
objective talk_to varrock_bartender

# 3. Bartender wants bandit orders as proof you cleared the road
objective item bandit_orders varrock_bartender

# 4. Return to Zaff with the news
objective talk_to varrock_trader

# 5. Travel to Al Kharid and talk to the silk merchant
objective talk_to alkharid_silk

# 6. Silk merchant wants a desert artifact (gives silk in exchange)
objective item desert_artifact alkharid_silk gives silk

# 7. Take the silk to Ali the spice trader
objective talk_to alkharid_spice

# 8. Ali wants the silk in exchange for spice
objective item silk alkharid_spice gives spice

# 9. Return to Hans with the goods
objective talk_to hans

# 10. Give Hans the spice to complete the trade route
objective item spice hans

# Rewards
reward_gil 500
reward_quest_points 3
reward_item iron_2h_sword

# === DIALOGUE ===

dialogue_start
Ah, adventurer! Just the person I was hoping to see.
I have an important task that requires someone brave and resourceful.
The three cities - Lumbridge, Varrock, and Al Kharid - need better trade routes.
Merchants are afraid to travel due to bandits and desert creatures.
I need you to establish connections with traders in each city.
Travel to Varrock first and speak with Zaff, the trader near the square.
Will you help establish these vital trade routes?
.

# Stage 1: Go to Varrock, talk to Zaff
dialogue_stage_1
Head north to Varrock and find Zaff near the central square.
Watch out for bandits on the road - they've been causing trouble lately.
Tell Zaff that Hans sent you to establish trade relations.
.

dialogue_turnin_1
Ah, you must be the one Hans mentioned!
I've been hoping to establish trade with Lumbridge for some time.
But first, we have a problem - bandits have been attacking our supply wagons.
The bartender at the Blue Moon Inn knows more about them.
Go speak with him - he's in the inn to the southeast of the square.
.

# Stage 2: Talk to the bartender
dialogue_stage_2
Find the bartender at the Blue Moon Inn, southeast of the square.
He may have information about the bandit attacks.
.

dialogue_turnin_2
You're looking into the bandit problem? Good, good.
Those scoundrels have been hitting wagons on the south road.
If you want to help, clear some of them out and bring me their orders.
That way we'll know what they're planning next.
The bandits lurk on the road between here and Lumbridge.
.

# Stage 3: Kill bandits, get orders
dialogue_stage_3
Hunt down the bandits on the road south of Varrock.
They sometimes carry orders - bring one back to the bartender.
The bandits are dangerous, so be prepared for a fight!
.

dialogue_turnin_3
Excellent work! Let me see those orders...
Hmm, this mentions a hideout in the eastern mountains.
I'll pass this to the city guards - they'll handle the rest.
Go tell Zaff the road should be safer now.
He'll want to proceed with the trade arrangements.
.

# Stage 4: Return to Zaff
dialogue_stage_4
Return to Zaff near the square and tell him the good news.
The road should be safer for trade now.
.

dialogue_turnin_4
The bandits have been dealt with? Excellent news!
Now we can proceed with establishing trade routes.
The next step is to connect with Al Kharid to the east.
They have the finest silk and spices in the land.
Travel there and speak with the Silk Merchant near the western stalls.
Be careful in the desert - scorpions and worse lurk there.
.

# Stage 5: Travel to Al Kharid, talk to silk merchant
dialogue_stage_5
Travel east to Al Kharid and find the Silk Merchant.
He should be near the trading stalls on the western side of the city.
Watch out for scorpions in the desert approach!
.

dialogue_turnin_5
Trade with Varrock and Lumbridge? How interesting!
I have the finest silk in all the desert, as you can see.
But I cannot simply give it away for a promise of trade.
Bring me something valuable - a desert artifact from the sand golems.
They guard ancient treasures in the deep desert to the southeast.
Bring me an artifact, and you shall have my best silk.
.

# Stage 6: Kill sand golems, get desert artifact
dialogue_stage_6
The sand golems are in the deep desert, southeast of Al Kharid.
They are powerful creatures - level 18, very dangerous!
Defeat one and retrieve a desert artifact for the Silk Merchant.
.

dialogue_turnin_6
A genuine desert artifact! Magnificent!
This is worth more than all the silk in my stall.
Here, take my finest rolls of silk - worth every thread.
Now, take this silk to Ali the Spice Trader near the furnace.
He loves quality silk and will trade generously for it.
.

# Stage 7: Take silk to Ali
dialogue_stage_7
Find Ali the Spice Trader near the furnace in Al Kharid.
He should be interested in trading for the silk.
.

dialogue_turnin_7
Is that silk from the Silk Merchant? Let me see...
Ah, this is the finest quality! I must have it!
I will trade you my most exotic spices for this silk.
These spices are worth a fortune in the northern cities.
Take them to your friend Hans in Lumbridge.
With silk and spice flowing, the trade route will be complete!
.

# Stage 8: Give Ali the silk
dialogue_stage_8
Give Ali the silk in exchange for his exotic spices.
He's eager to make the trade.
.

dialogue_turnin_8
The deal is done! Here are the spices - the finest in the desert.
Cinnamon, saffron, and rare peppers from far eastern lands.
Hans will be thrilled to receive these.
Return to Lumbridge and complete the trading expedition!
The three cities will prosper from this new route.
.

# Stage 9: Return to Hans
dialogue_stage_9
Return to Lumbridge and speak with Hans.
He'll be eager to hear about your expedition!
.

dialogue_turnin_9
You've returned! Tell me everything!
Zaff in Varrock... the bandits cleared... the Silk Merchant...
Desert artifacts... Ali's spices... this is wonderful news!
Give me those spices and we'll make it official.
The Trading Expedition will be a resounding success!
.

# Stage 10: Turn in the spice
dialogue_stage_10
Give Hans the spices to complete the Trading Expedition.
This will establish the trade route between all three cities.
.

dialogue_turnin_10
The spices! They smell magnificent!
With this, the trade route between Lumbridge, Varrock, and Al Kharid is complete!
Merchants can now travel safely between all three cities.
You've done an incredible service to the realm, adventurer.
Here is your reward - 500 gold, 3 quest points, and this fine iron blade!
The people of all three cities will remember your deeds.
.

dialogue_complete
The trade routes you established are flourishing!
Merchants speak highly of your deeds across all three cities.
Silk and spices flow freely, and the bandits have been scattered.
Perhaps one day there will be another grand expedition...
.
